blocks.en:
TRELLIS uses TRELLIS-500K; TripoSG uses curated Objaverse(-XL) and ShapeNet data.
PartCrafter uses part-annotated Objaverse, ShapeNet, and ABO data; PartPacker uses filtered/extracted parts from TRELLIS-500K/Objaverse-XL;
OmniPart uses self-constructed part-labeled data with a TRELLIS-based backbone. FullPart trains on PartVerseXL and is omitted on that benchmark. Our PartVerseXL evaluation set is strictly held out, whereas PartObjaverse-Tiny shares Objaverse asset lineage with several pretrained methods, including our TripoSG initialization.

blocks.zh:
TRELLIS使用TRELLIS-500K;TripoSG使用被管理Objaverse(-XL)和ShapeNet数据.
PartCrafter使用部分附加说明的Objaverse、ShapeNet和ABO数据;PartPacker使用TRELLIS-500K/Objaverse-XL的过滤/提取部件;
OmniPart使用自构的带有TRELLIS主干线的部分标签数据. PartVerseXL上的全编列车在该基准上被省略. 我们的PartVerseXL评价集被严格保留,而PartObjaverse-Tiny则通过几种事先经过训练的方法分享Objaverse资产系列,包括我们的TripoSG初始化.

blocks.en:
Point Sampling Strategies. We consider four representative strategies to simulate diverse user behaviors and annotation noise:
1). Center , the centroid of the part mask;
2). Edge , a point sampled near the part boundary to induce maximal spatial ambiguity;
3). Offset , a randomly perturbed centroid to mimic typical user imprecision;
4). Cluster , the patch center nearest the object’s geometric center.

